# Default owners for normal changes to this repo (adapter code, tests, tooling).
# These teams can review and approve day-to-day pull requests.
* @smartcontractkit/data-feeds-engineers @smartcontractkit/data-streams-engineers @smartcontractkit/data-sourcing

# Release artifacts left without an owner, on purpose.
# A release PR also touches changesets and every package's manifest/changelog. If
# those paths were owned by a team, "Require review from Code Owners" would demand
# a second approval from that team on top of the release approvers below. No owner
# here means the normal write-access approval applies, and the release approvers
# remain the only code-owner requirement.
# These patterns must stay ABOVE /package.json - last match wins.
/.changeset/
**/package.json
**/README.md
**/CHANGELOG.md

# --- EA release gate ---------------------------------------------------------
# "Require review from Code Owners" is enabled on main. It is evaluated per
# changed file: every changed file that has an owner needs an approval from one
# of *that file's* owners. It is not "any code owner of the PR".
#
# Every file below therefore needs an approval from @b16z-sc or @walked08860.
# Keep these lines exclusive: adding a team to one of them makes that team's
# approval sufficient for the file.

# Publish triggers. release.yml + deploy.yml fire on a MASTERLIST.md push to main
# (GH release, private ECR, dispatch to infra-k8s); publish.yml fires on a
# public-adapter-versions.yml push (public ECR -> node operators).
/MASTERLIST.md @b16z-sc @walked08860
/public-adapter-versions.yml @b16z-sc @walked08860
/package.json @b16z-sc @walked08860

# The release machinery itself. Editing these is equivalent to releasing, so they
# go through the same approvers. (/.github/actions/setup is also used by
# publish.yml but is shared with CI and deliberately not gated here.)
/.github/workflows/release.yml @b16z-sc @walked08860
/.github/workflows/deploy.yml @b16z-sc @walked08860
/.github/workflows/publish.yml @b16z-sc @walked08860
/.github/workflows/create-public-versions-pr.yml @b16z-sc @walked08860
/.github/actions/create-ecrs/ @b16z-sc @walked08860

# The gate itself, so it cannot be re-owned in an unrelated PR.
/.github/CODEOWNERS @b16z-sc @walked08860
